&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Top 2 Comments:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style="margin: 10px 0; padding: 10px; background: #f6f6f6; border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 5px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Esophagus4:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0;"&gt;AWS has theirs as well: &lt;a href="https:&amp;#x2F;&amp;#x2F;awslabs.github.io&amp;#x2F;mcp&amp;#x2F;servers&amp;#x2F;aws-documentation-mcp-server" rel="nofollow"&gt;https:&amp;#x2F;&amp;#x2F;awslabs.github.io&amp;#x2F;mcp&amp;#x2F;servers&amp;#x2F;aws-documentation-mcp-...&lt;/a&gt;&lt;p&gt;As it turns out these are very helpful for obscure features and settings buried in the documentation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style="margin: 10px 0; padding: 10px; background: #f6f6f6; border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 5px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;er4hn:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0;"&gt;This must be what gwern meant when he said to write for AI.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
